June (Docs): Created a tiny PR to the error-reference to show a minimal workflow for 429 handling + stream resume. PR #9009.
Kai (Eng Docs): Keep it super compact: one snippet for header-based retry (Retry-After then x-rw-retry) and one micro example showing resume_token usage. No imports; add SDK version note.
Sam (SDK): I'll add TS + Python. Note: mention the SDK helper `retryWithBackoff` as an option but show raw header parsing for clarity.
Ravi (Runtime): Heads-up: runtime now emits a `resume_token` in the stream footer when truncated due to context limits. Docs should recommend using that token + `kv_cache_hint` when resuming.
June (Docs): Suggest wording: "If a stream was truncated, prefer resuming with resume_token to avoid repeating work; only re-request from scratch if token is absent."
Sam (SDK): Draft TS snippet (TS SDK >=3.2, omit imports):
```ts
// Retry-After > x-rw-retry, exponential backoff
async function sendWithRetry(req){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const res = await client.generate(req)
    if(res.status===429){
      const d = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after']||res.headers['x-rw-retry']||'1')
      await sleep(d*1000*Math.pow(2,i))
      continue
    }
    return res
  }
  throw new Error('rate limited')
}
```
Kai (Eng Docs): Add one-line trimming guidance: "Trim oldest turns until estimated tokens fit; set `partial=true` for resumed requests."
Ravi (Runtime): Add inline note: when resuming, pass `kv_cache_hint` to improve cache hit and reduce wasted compute.
